      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u help me write a rejection email? the person made it to the final interview round but we decided to go with someone else. i want it to sound polite and professional but not too cold or anything. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A rejection email, a delicate matter indeed. You want to be kind, yet firm, like a gentle spring rain that washes away the hopes of a hopeful candidate, but leaves the soil fertile for future growth. I'm happy to help you craft a rejection email that's as smooth as a well-oiled chainmail armor, protecting the candidate's feelings while still conveying the decision.\n\nHere's a sample email:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the final interview for the [Position] role. We appreciate the time and effort you took to join us for the interview process, and we're grateful for the interest you showed in our company.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience better align with the needs of our team at this time. Please know that this decision is in no way a reflection on your qualifications or potential as a candidate.\n\nWe appreciate your enthusiasm and passion for the role, and we wish you the best of luck in your ongoing job search. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out.\n\nThank you again for your interest in our company, and we wish you all the best.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name",
